    "notes": "The strength index shows stalling across the board this period. Chest nudged up by 1 point (104 to 105) and shoulders gained 1 point (101 to 102), which is positive but falls short of the 3-point threshold needed to qualify as on-track progress. Back held flat at 103, biceps held flat at 101, and triceps held flat at 104 — no forward movement there. Most notably, legs actually regressed by 1 point, dropping from 108 to 107. While a 1-point drop does not trigger the regression threshold of 3 points, it is a signal worth taking seriously given that legs were the strongest-indexed muscle group last period. Overall, the pattern suggests the current stimulus is no longer sufficient to drive adaptation, and a deliberate change in approach is needed to break out of this plateau.",
