  "actionItems": [
    "Introduce a small progressive overload stimulus on your main compound lifts — try adding a small amount of weight or one additional rep to at least one set per session on back and legs, where the index is flat or declining.",
    "Prioritize leg training earlier in the week when energy is freshest, since the legs index has dipped and lower-body compound work is especially valuable for overall strength goals.",
    "Add one extra set of direct biceps work to close the gap between your pulling volume (6 sets of back) and elbow flexor volume (3 sets of biceps), which will better support your back training over time.",
    "Review whether your rep ranges and rest periods on the flat or stalling muscle groups are optimized for strength — for a strength-focused goal, working in the 3 to 6 rep range with longer rest periods on primary lifts tends to drive strength index progress more effectively than higher-rep work."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strength indices stalled across most muscle groups this period with legs dipping 1 point; volume coverage is decent but legs and biceps are relatively undertrained, and the primary focus next period should be breaking the plateau through deliberate overload on compound lifts."
}
